{{!
    @template tool_vae/remove_record_leaves

    What leaves with the row of a record that is removed: a sentence, then one line per kind, with its count; the addresses
    of the record listed under their line. On one logical line, each break carried by a comment.

    Every text comes from the context, worded by tool_vae\output\remove_record_leaves. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * leaves - string, the sentence that opens the list
    * items - list of {text, refs}: each line; refs is null, or {addresses}: the addresses under the line, each {title, url}

    Example context (json):
    {
        "leaves": "What leaves with the row:",
        "items": [
            {"text": "Licence: Licence Ouverte, France Compétences", "refs": null},
            {"text": "2 address(es):", "refs": {"addresses": [{"title": "Fiche", "url": "https://example.com/fiche"} ] } }
        ]
    }
}}
<p class="mb-1">{{leaves}}</p><ul class="tool-vae-removal">{{#items}}<li>{{text}}{{#refs}}<ul>{{!
}}{{#addresses}}<li>{{title}} ({{url}})</li>{{/addresses}}</ul>{{/refs}}</li>{{/items}}</ul>
